The god will do you a bunch of good things, like:

@ Increase your luck ("You glimpse a four-leaf clover")

@ Grant you an artifact or spellbook ("An object appears at your feet!")

@ Decrease your prayer timeout ("You have a hopeful feeling")

and by praying, you can get things like

@ Holy water (you need to be standing on an altar onto which you
  dropped potions of uncursed/cursed water)

@ Intrinsics ("...I grant thee the gift of [something]!")

@ HP increase ("You are surrounded by a golden glow")

@ Crowned Hand of Elbereth etc. ("I crown thee....the [blah blah]")

You'll always get holy water after your prayer timeout expires (you
don't see the "you have a hopeful feeling" anymore when you
sacrifice).  For other praying effects, you need to have sacrificed
enough since your timeout expired or have waited very long (I'm not
sure about this one), and you don't need to be standing on the altar.

There are drawbacks though.  One, the HoE etc. thing increases your
prayer timeout A LOT while granting you fire/cold/poison resistance,
see invisible and a weapon artifact depending on your class, so if you
already have all the intrinsics and an appropriate weapon, you won't
like that.

Also, the chance of wishing for an artifact goes bang-low after seeing
three (I think) or more artifacts in the game, so if you are planning
to wish for a bPYEC or Stormy or whatever using the WoW in the castle,
you may not want to sacrifice too much before you get there, to keep
the artifact count low.

